.github.com/users/DaGromflomite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaGromflomite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaGromflomite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":61,"digest":"sha256:6d81f5b0e747c96d5f3487c7b769ec5a3b79cbfbb0f80a92f32167ee7b4d1951","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-11-01T03:14:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T03:14:45Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/DaGromflomite/SleazyCrow/releases/download/v1.2.0-beta/SleazyCrow-v1.2.0-beta.apk.md5"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DaGromflomite/SleazyCrow/tarball/v1.2.0-beta","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DaGromflomite/SleazyCrow/zipball/v1.2.0-beta","body":"# Sleazy Crow v1.2.0-beta\r\n\r\n> ⚠ **BETA — for testing.** If it doesn't work on your Evil Crow, go back to [Senape3000's official firmware](https://senape3000.github.io/EvilCrowRF-V2/web-flasher/) and please [report what happened](https://github.com/DaGromflomite/SleazyCrow/issues/new).\r\n\r\nSleazy Crow is a community fork of [Senape3000's EvilCrowRF-V2](https://github.com/Senape3000/EvilCrowRF-V2) firmware and app for the Evil Crow RF V2 (MIT license).\r\n\r\n## Install\r\n- **Web flasher (easiest):** https://dagromflomite.github.io/SleazyCrow/ — desktop Chrome/Edge/Opera.\r\n- **App:** install `SleazyCrow-v1.2.0-beta.apk` on Android. It installs as a separate app (\"Sleazy Crow\") next to the official one.\r\n- **esptool:** `esptool --chip esp32 erase-flash` then `esptool --chip esp32 --baud 921600 write-flash 0x0 sleazycrow-fw-v1.2.0-beta-full.bin`\r\n- **OTA from the app:** the app finds `sleazycrow-fw-v1.2.0-beta-OTA.bin` automatically.\r\n\r\n## Firmware changes\r\n- **feature**: Sleazy Crow: community fork of Senape3000's EvilCrowRF-V2 firmware (based on v1.1.3). Bluetooth name is now SleazyCrow.\r\n- **fix**: Bluetooth no longer drops ~12 s after connecting on Android: incoming commands run on their own task and stable connection parameters are requested.\r\n- **fix**: No boot crash when built with Arduino core 3.3.x (BLE controller memory was freed before NimBLE started).\r\n- **fix**: Toolchain and NimBLE pinned so every build is identical (fixes the 'adc_oneshot.h' compile error).\r\n- **fix**: File uploads: a full queue no longer drops chunks, and missing/out-of-order chunks fail with an error instead of saving a corrupted file.\r\n- **fix**: ProtoPirate decode results show the protocol type name instead of a number.\r\n- **improvement**: Boot log prints the firmware name, version and upstream project.\r\n\r\n## App changes\r\n- **feature**: Sleazy Crow app: installs alongside the official EvilCrow RF app; updates come from the Sleazy Crow releases.\r\n- **feature**: Flipper Sub-GHz DB: pick which sections to copy to the SD card instead of the whole database; brute-force folders are opt-in.\r\n- **feature**: Optional 'format SD card first' and an explainer before the download.\r\n- **fix**: Large RAW .sub files are split into smaller pieces so they upload reliably (playback is identical).\r\n- **fix**: Uploads no longer report false failures ('Null check operator' race).\r\n- **improvement**: Uploads about 40x faster; live time-remaining estimate.\r\n- **feature**: Transmit button toggles continuous transmission on/off.\r\n- **feature**: Brute force: US/EU frequency choice and timing (te) override.\r\n- **improvement**: File preview loads only when requested, so opening files is instant.\r\n\r\nChecksums: each file has a matching `.md5`.\r\n"}]